ment used in the treatment of mitochondrial disorders, including MNGIE, to support cellular energy production.", "L-CARNITINA:L-CARNITINA, also known as L-carnitine, is an amino acid that plays a crucial role in energy metabolism. It is often included in infant formulas to support the energy needs of infants. Additionally, L-carnitine is utilized as a dietary supplement to assist in managing symptoms associated with mitochondrial diseases, such as MNGIE. In cancer patients, L-carnitine may help increase body weight and enhance overall quality of life. Furthermore, it is recognized for its benefits in optimizing weight and body composition among athletes. L-carnitine is also important in the treatment of β-oxidation disorders, as it aids in the transport of fatty acids into the mitochondria for energy production.", "ANTIDIABÉTICOS ORALES:Oral antidiabetic medications are prescribed to manage the patient's diabetes, which is complicated by mitochondrial dysfunction.", "REPAGLINIDA:Repaglinide is another oral antidiabetic medication prescribed to the patient to help control blood sugar levels.", "AMAUROSIS:Amaurosis is a condition affecting the patient, complicating their ability to self-administer insulin.", "CUIDADORA PRINCIPAL:The primary caregiver, who is the patient's mother, assists in managing the patient's treatment and understanding insulin dosage adjustments.", "TRASPLANTE DE CÉLULAS HEMATOPIÉTICAS:Hematopoietic cell transplantation, also known as stem cell transplantation, is a medical procedure designed to restore blood cell production in patients suffering from specific diseases. This treatment involves the transplantation of hematopoietic stem cells, which are crucial for generating blood cells. Although hematopoietic stem cell transplantation was considered as a treatment option for the patient, it was ultimately rejected.", "MERCEDES VÁZQUEZ GUTIÉRREZ:Dr. Mercedes Vázquez Gutiérrez is a specialist in endocrinology and nutrition at the Hospital Universitario de Torrecárdenas in Almería. She is actively involved in providing nutritional support for renal patients, demonstrating her expertise in both endocrinology and nutrition within the healthcare setting.", "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO DE TORRECÁRDENAS:Hospital Universitario de Torrecárdenas is a clinical unit specializing in Endocrinology and Nutrition located in Almería.", "UCI:The Unidad de Cuidados Intensivos (UCI), also known as the Intensive Care Unit, is a specialized area within a hospital dedicated to providing intensive medical care to critically ill patients. This unit is equipped to handle a variety of severe medical conditions, including but not limited to severe pancreatitis and acute renal failure. Patients in the UCI receive close monitoring and specialized treatment tailored to their critical health needs. The UCI plays a crucial role in managing complications and ensuring that patients in critical condition receive the necessary care to stabilize their health.", "DUODENOPANCREATECTOMÍA SUBTOTAL:Subtotal duodenopancreatectomy is the surgical procedure performed on the patient to address the pancreatic tumor.", "BIOPSIA:BIOPSIA refers to a medical procedure involving the extraction of tissue for diagnostic purposes. In one instance, a biopsy was performed via endoscopic ultrasound to confirm the diagnosis of a pancreatic mucinous tumor. Additionally, the term encompasses intestinal biopsy, which is a diagnostic procedure that involves the removal of tissue from the small intestine to assess damage caused by celiac disease. Thus, BIOPSIA encompasses various types of biopsies used to diagnose different conditions, including pancreatic tumors and intestinal disorders.", "SANGRADO MASIVO:Massive bleeding occurred post-surgery, necessitating urgent intervention for the patient.", "DEHISCENCIA DE LA ANASTOMOSIS PANCREATOYEYUNAL:Dehiscence of the pancreatojejunostomy occurred, leading to further complications for the patient."], "parameters": {"model": "text-e